    </div>

    <div class="prose-tca">

      <p>I'm Jackson Christopher — 6'4", Mechanical Engineering senior at UC Berkeley. For most of my undergraduate years, I had a persistent shoulder tension problem that I'd been managing with heat packs and ignoring. Both shoulders, worse on the right, worse after long study sessions. I assumed it was just part of sitting at a desk for hours.</p>
      <p>It wasn't until I started studying ergonomics from an engineering perspective — force diagrams, moment arms, muscle fatigue mechanics — that I understood what was actually happening. My chairs were too small for my body, and my trapezius muscles were paying for it every single day. This page is what I wish I'd read three years earlier.</p>

      <!-- TL;DR -->
